  "independent_findings": [
    "Own isFood excludes symbolic howling foods; hand mobInteract calls super first, then own tagged branch emits EAT/sound and crafting remainder request before noncreative shrink1, and sets animation. No own server guard or durable payer/output receipt. Tag contents absent; do not assert rotten flesh or any actual survival input.",
    "Dropped-item helper excludes occupied hand/mounts, samples eligible item age>30 with radius9cube, follows target with own cooldown, and callback-before-shrink1 occurs only at alive target and squared distance<2. Sink does not repeat every original qualification/delay/owner check. Own dropped meat heals5, bone converts; neither path directly starts HOWL. Shared helper and species difference each0.",
    "ANIMATION_HOWL tick>3 is outside server-only attack/sit branch and resets scareMobsTime40 every eligible update. Each such processing sees40, triggers modulo5 navigation each refresh update and ends39. Once refresh stops, remaining39 counter updates are not total animation/world/wall duration. Handler engine unexpanded; currentAnimation has no own initializer, and setAnimation does not reset animationTick or sittingTime. No lasting immunity or guaranteed animation start/finish.",
    "Local Monster.class box inflate16,8,16 has no own radial/LOS/ownership restriction and defaults NO_SPECTATORS. Mob.setTarget(null) dispatches cancellable/rewritable Forge event; it can retain/replace target. setLastHurtByMob(null) changes that field and timestamp, not player-hurt field or future reacquisition. No actual targeting/escape guarantee.",
    "LandRandomPos directional sampling considers up to10 candidate evaluations and world limits/restriction/navigation stability, solid lift, water and malus. It can return null; PathNavigation.moveTo returns false on null/done/empty path and caller ignores boolean. Requested destination is not safe accepted path or actual movement.",
    "Bone conversion constructs one BONE_MEAL ItemStack and requests spawn exactly3 times on normal returns because nextInt(1)=0. Same stack is passed each time. Native constructor->setItem->SynchedEntityData set/DataItem.setValue show no stack copy in that route; entities can share reference/representation. captureDrops/default pickup delay/unchecked add remain; no three independent admitted outputs, player ownership/pickup or duplication exploit demonstrated.",
    "Own void killed(ServerLevel,LivingEntity) is distinct from boolean killedEntity native hook. Current bounded cache search has no explicit caller of own method. Native death hook can be canceled, then sourceEntity.killedEntity gates deathloot. Animal/UNDEAD bone reward branch therefore not established as wired to native kill. Attack requests at animationtick5 and doHurtTarget true do not prove damage/death.",
    "No own save override for animation/scare/sitting timers; inherited Animal stores InLove/LoveCause and not these paid-intent fields. Fresh object defaults differ from applying inherited read to an existing object. No complete inherited/capability/world reconstruction or refund/replay guarantee.",
    "One whole bounded behavior differs from persistent attempt-latched alarm encounter, shoreline retained-food custody/owner assignment, and externally funded facility shared crop service: a fed actor requests transient nearby target clearing and retreat with asymmetric hand-versus-ground processing. Multiple animations/helpers/defects/sounds/supportlines count0. Global/migration novelty unestablished0; ecological policy maximum1 only."
  ],
  "mandatory_constraints": [
    "Complete317-line actor plus actual registry/attributes/placement, symbolic howling tag factory and config defaults/load assignments are read. CREATURE registration and placement hooks are supporting context only, not deployed biome spawning, cap or actual population proof.",
    "Only one proposed whole feeding-mediated temporary local target-clear/retreat policy. Manual mobInteract delegates super BEFORE own tag branch, then game-event/sound and crafting-remainder spawn attempt BEFORE noncreative shrink1; starts HOWL if current animation is not HOWL. Own branch has no explicit server guard or durable paid queue. Tagged howling foods are excluded from own breeding isFood, but not from dropped-item edible meat predicate.",
    "Dropped-item callback in previously actually read CreatureAITargetItems precedes target stack shrink1. Own canTargetItem admits edible meat or exact BONE; onGetItem bone requests conversion, other eligible food requests heal5 and does NOT start HOWL. These paths are distinct; dropped howling food is not proved to howl. Reused helper earns0.",
    "Actual own HOWL branch lies outside server-only attack/sit block; tick>3 resets scareMobsTime40 on every eligible update, so processing sees40 and satisfies modulo5 EVERY refresh update, then decrements to39. Following cessation of refresh, the39 remaining positive-counter updates do not establish39 wall/world ticks or total animation duration. AnimationHandler/updateAnimations and IAnimatedEntity/Animation Citadel source absent in checked local roots; no framework clock/initialization/reload proof.",
    "Query uses Monster.class and bbox.inflate(16,8,16), default EntityGetter NO_SPECTATORS, no own radial/LOS/species/ownership filter. setTarget(null) delegates cancellable/rewritable Forge target event; no guarantee final target null. setLastHurtByMob(null) clears that field and updates timestamp; player-hurt field separate. Later AI reacquisition remains possible; this is no sustained immunity.",
    "LandRandomPos.getPosAway is directional candidate sampling with world/restriction/stability/up-out-of-solid/water/malus gates. Nullable result and PathNavigation boolean failure exist; caller ignores moveTo result. No accepted safe path, actual movement, reachability or escape duration certified. Prior actual RandomPos/GoalUtils source reading reused0.",
    "Bone conversion creates ONE ItemStack(BONE_MEAL), then3+random.nextInt(1) means exactly3 loop calls on normal return, all pass SAME stack reference. Entity.spawnAtLocation passes it to ItemEntity; constructor->setItem->SynchedEntityData.set->DataItem.setValue carries reference without shown copy. Requests may alias; default pickup delay/captureDrops/unchecked add and no thrower owner remain. This is not three accepted independent outputs or pickup proof; no runtime duplication/loss exploit claimed.",
    "Void killed(ServerLevel,LivingEntity) lacks @Override and differs from native boolean killedEntity. Bounded complete-AM Java call/declaration search finds only that declaration, no explicit .killed( caller. Actual LivingEntity.die invokes sourceEntity.killedEntity; native Entity.killedEntity returns true. Thus this study cannot claim the proposed Animal/UNDEAD random bone drop is bound to native kill lifecycle. External reflection/other unseen callers not universally excluded.",
    "Complete class has no own add/readAdditionalSaveData override for howl/scare/sitting timers. Inherited Animal state is not a durable paid howl receipt. Fresh constructor state differs from invoking inherited read on existing object; no clear-everything/reload/refund claim. setAnimation sets current and for howl sitting and max>=25, but does not itself reset sittingTime or animationTick; external handler unexpanded.",
    "Attack animation requests damage at own tick5 with target and LOS in server guard, doHurtTarget merely starts animation/returns true. No explicit successful damage/death receipt, no ownership/output acquisition or native kill credit. Damage hooks and full world/entity lifecycle outside scope.",
    "Pinned tree contains howling-food JSON blob d73d41ac63d938741f5f22809d431a11b3813497/70B, raw missing in selected root. No rotten-flesh/member/nonempty tag or default survival input claim. Config source defaults10/0 and load assignments do not prove current installed values.",
    "Local source identity binds metadata/tree and raw Git blobs, not fresh remote commit authentication. One original source-study proposal only; independent main semantic review still needed, dependency gaps cannot be erased by source ranges, animation constants, species or defect counting."
  ],
